 ### What Good Looks Like
 
 | Scenario | Expected behavior |
 | --- | --- |
 | Cold build | Complete required outputs, including compilation and required generation. This is the full-work baseline for the recorded cache state. |
 | Warm build | Changed inputs and affected dependencies invalidate the appropriate work; unrelated recompilation needs explanation. |
-| No-op build | Up-to-date expensive compilation/generation skips. Under roughly 5 seconds for small repositories or 30 seconds for large ones can be useful triage hints, not universal budgets. |
+| No-op build | Up-to-date expensive compilation/generation skips. Compare its duration with this repository's own repeated warm and cold samples. |
 
 **Red flags to investigate, not automatic diagnoses:**
-- No-op build over 30 seconds: distinguish evaluation, restore, copying, and
-  unexpected execution before applying [incremental fixes](incremental-build.md).
+- No-op time repeatedly close to warm or cold time: distinguish evaluation, restore,
+  copying, and unexpected execution before applying [incremental fixes](incremental-build.md).
 - Warm build recompiles everything: inspect the input/API change and dependency
   chain; do not assume every downstream rebuild is unnecessary.
 - Long cold restore: investigate feed/network work and cache state, not just
   package-cache problems.
 
+Do not use universal duration or percentage thresholds to declare a bottleneck:
+the seconds and percentages in [build-perf-diagnostics.md](build-perf-diagnostics.md)
+are starting hints for where to look, not pass/fail thresholds. Rank costs
+against the controlled samples and the build's own target and task timings.
+
+### Capture analyzer evidence
+
+A binlog records compiler and task timing, but per-analyzer timing needs an
+analyzer-reporting run. When the SDK and compiler support it, capture one under
+an unused name:
+
+```powershell
+dotnet build -m "-bl:analyzers-01.binlog" -p:ReportAnalyzer=true
+```
+
+[Replay the log](binlog-failure-analysis.md#replay-a-binary-log) and read the
+analyzer execution-time report that the compiler task logged, searched as in
+[performance diagnostics](build-perf-diagnostics.md). If granular timing is
+unavailable, compare otherwise identical samples with `-p:RunAnalyzers=false` as
+an attribution experiment; do not present disabling analyzers as the fix.
+Preserve analyzer enforcement in CI.
+
